# Walkthrough: Compacted Video Context for AI

I have implemented a new "Compacted Context" output format that allows you to "compress" lecture videos into a high-density Markdown format. This format is optimized for AI context windows, ensuring that both visual information and transcripts are preserved in a concise manner.

## Changes Made

### Output Formatter
Updated [src/services/output_formatter.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/services/output_formatter.py) to include:
- [format_compacted](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/services/output_formatter.py#96-135): A new method that generates a dense Markdown string.
- Updated [save_outputs](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/services/output_formatter.py#136-186): Now automatically saves a `.compact.md` file alongside the standard JSON and Markdown outputs.

## Format Overview

The compacted format uses a dense structure:
- **Header**: Contains the lecture title, job ID, and extraction method.
- **Topics**: Lists detected topics for quick context.
- **Segments**:
  - Timestamps in `[START-END]` format.
  - Visual summaries integrated into the header.
  - Full transcripts for the segment.
  - OCR text (if it provides additional info beyond the visual summary) as blockquotes.

## Verification Results

I verified the implementation using a test script with mock video processing data.

### Test Output Preview

```markdown
# COMPACTED CONTEXT: lecture_video.mp4
## ID: test_job_123 | METHOD: multimodal
## TOPICS: Mathematics, Calculus
## CONTENT
### [0:00:00-0:00:20] | VISUALS: Slide showing 'Welcome to Calculus 101'
Hello everyone, today we will start with the basics of derivatives.
```

The verification script confirmed:
- ✅ Correct generation of the compacted Markdown string.
- ✅ Correct saving of the `.compact.md` file in the output directory.
- ✅ Inclusion of transcripts, visual summaries, and OCR data.

You can now use these `.compact.md` files as a highly efficient way to provide lecture context to AI!
